1
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:12,744
I’m sorry for the trouble earlier, Comrade Roong.

2
00:00:12,745 --> 00:00:14,064
Especially now that Comrade Fah has forbidden-

3
00:00:14,065 --> 00:00:15,224
-anyone from entering or leaving the base.

4
00:00:15,225 --> 00:00:16,984
But that household is in serious condition.

5
00:00:16,985 --> 00:00:18,904
That’s why we had to ask you to come help.

6
00:00:18,905 --> 00:00:21,464
It’s alright. The villagers’ lives are what matter most.

7
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:23,761
If there’s any problem, I’ll speak with Comrade Fah myself.

8
00:00:23,785 --> 00:00:24,944
Um... Comrade Roong.

9
00:00:24,945 --> 00:00:25,945
We’d better go this way.

10
00:00:25,946 --> 00:00:28,081
There are too many people that way. Someone might see us.

11
00:00:28,105 --> 00:00:30,345
If we go this way, we won’t run into Comrade Fah either.

12
00:00:37,385 --> 00:00:39,225
Ever since Comrade Ploeng died,

13
00:00:39,785 --> 00:00:41,305
the base has felt so quiet and lonely.

14
00:00:43,225 --> 00:00:45,025
How has Comrade Bai Tong been lately?

15
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:48,705
She barely ate foods I gave her.

16
00:00:51,585 --> 00:00:52,585
Comrade Gaun Hin.

17
00:00:52,985 --> 00:00:54,064
Where are you going?

18
00:00:54,065 --> 00:00:56,024
Oh, I’m taking documents for the courier-

19
00:00:56,025 --> 00:00:57,505
-to deliver for printing in the city.

20
00:00:58,385 --> 00:00:59,385
Go and come back quickly.

21
00:00:59,585 --> 00:01:00,585
Be careful.

22
00:01:02,945 --> 00:01:03,945
Comrades

23
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,024
we caught the person who killed Ploeng.

24
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:07,104
Comrades.

25
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:09,505
Comrades, we caught the person who killed Ploeng.

26
00:01:57,385 --> 00:01:58,665
Mm.

27
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:04,625
Dan.

28
00:02:07,945 --> 00:02:09,385
Answer whatever I ask.

29
00:02:09,985 --> 00:02:11,545
Because if you talk,

30
00:02:13,025 --> 00:02:14,224
you won’t have to get hurt.

31
00:02:14,225 --> 00:02:15,225
Mm.

32
00:02:15,305 --> 00:02:16,305
Comrade Fah! Comrade Fah!

33
00:02:16,825 --> 00:02:17,825
Comrade Fah.

34
00:02:18,385 --> 00:02:19,385
Comrade Fah.

35
00:02:20,545 --> 00:02:21,904
Comrade Roong is gone.

36
00:02:21,905 --> 00:02:23,065
Since when?

37
00:02:23,585 --> 00:02:24,545
Yang Sue said

38
00:02:24,545 --> 00:02:25,465
a villager was in critical condition

39
00:02:25,465 --> 00:02:26,385
and urgently needed medicine.

40
00:02:26,386 --> 00:02:27,626
So Roong rushed out right away.

41
00:02:29,025 --> 00:02:30,425
I told her to stay inside the base.

42
00:02:31,905 --> 00:02:33,264
And where is Yang Sue now?

43
00:02:33,265 --> 00:02:35,424
The villagers said he left with the cabbage truck

44
00:02:35,425 --> 00:02:36,665
before sunrise.

45
00:02:38,745 --> 00:02:40,065
And now Comrade Roong is missing.

46
00:02:40,745 --> 00:02:41,825
Don’t tell anyone yet.

47
00:02:44,865 --> 00:02:46,785
I don’t want the people in the village to panic.

48
00:02:55,585 --> 00:02:56,065
Whoa...

49
00:02:56,545 --> 00:02:57,705
that was close.

50
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,265
Just now, Comrade Yue seemed to turn

51
00:03:00,266 --> 00:03:01,544
and look this way too.

52
00:03:01,545 --> 00:03:03,105
Not sure if he saw us or not.

53
00:03:04,745 --> 00:03:06,585
Sorry, I lost myself for a second.

54
00:03:08,185 --> 00:03:08,825
This guy...

55
00:03:08,826 --> 00:03:10,624
he’s probably the one who killed Comrade Ploeng.

56
00:03:10,625 --> 00:03:12,144
You know him too?

57
00:03:12,145 --> 00:03:13,065
Yes.

58
00:03:13,066 --> 00:03:14,506
He was my neighbor when I was a kid.

59
00:03:16,345 --> 00:03:18,384
Doesn’t matter how you know him.

60
00:03:18,385 --> 00:03:20,064
You’d better stay away from him.

61
00:03:20,065 --> 00:03:21,625
You might get dragged into it too.

62
00:03:23,145 --> 00:03:24,705
Hey, Comrade Saeng.

63
00:03:24,985 --> 00:03:27,425
Don’t even think about going to see Dan, Comrade Saeng.

64
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,105
Go on, get going.

65
00:03:45,265 --> 00:03:46,625
What brings you here, Comrade?

66
00:03:47,425 --> 00:03:49,345
Or do you need some medicine?

67
00:03:50,465 --> 00:03:52,905
I came to get supplies to treat the prisoner’s gunshot wound.

68
00:03:53,305 --> 00:03:54,345
Get them ready for me.

69
00:03:55,865 --> 00:03:56,865
Yes.

70
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:13,304
And...

71
00:04:13,305 --> 00:04:15,864
Are you going to remove the bullet yourself?

72
00:04:15,865 --> 00:04:17,425
Would you like me to do it for you?

73
00:04:19,265 --> 00:04:20,265
It’s alright.

74
00:04:21,585 --> 00:04:22,585
I’ll take it out myself.

75
00:04:30,745 --> 00:04:31,745
Comrade Yue.

76
00:04:33,385 --> 00:04:34,385
Comrade Ying.

77
00:04:34,705 --> 00:04:36,064
I came to speak with you about-

78
00:04:36,065 --> 00:04:37,505
-my mother’s condition for a moment.

79
00:04:39,585 --> 00:04:40,585
How is she?

80
00:04:40,985 --> 00:04:42,025
Has she gotten any better?

81
00:04:43,065 --> 00:04:44,265
We got medicine from the base,

82
00:04:44,905 --> 00:04:46,345
so we’ve managed to keep her stable.

83
00:04:53,585 --> 00:04:54,625
It’s done.

84
00:04:58,945 --> 00:05:01,024
Has he admitted yet that he was-

85
00:05:01,025 --> 00:05:02,425
-the one who killed Comrade Ploeng?

86
00:05:07,465 --> 00:05:08,465
Not yet.

87
00:06:09,865 --> 00:06:11,865
A son of a high-ranking military officer like you.

88
00:06:13,425 --> 00:06:15,705
Why would you choose to be stationed here?

89
00:06:17,465 --> 00:06:18,785
What do you want?

90
00:06:34,545 --> 00:06:36,345
Getting yourself captured like this...

91
00:06:39,025 --> 00:06:40,145
Was it your plan?

92
00:06:58,145 --> 00:06:59,905
Comrade Roong disappearance...

93
00:07:02,545 --> 00:07:04,105
That was because of you too, wasn’t it?

94
00:07:44,745 --> 00:07:46,185
Whatever you’re hoping for,

95
00:07:49,825 --> 00:07:51,385
you won’t get your way.

96
00:07:54,225 --> 00:07:55,225
You still don’t know

97
00:07:56,825 --> 00:07:58,305
who’s going to be disappointed.

98
00:08:45,545 --> 00:08:46,345
Vin.

99
00:08:46,345 --> 00:08:47,345
Dan.

100
00:08:53,905 --> 00:08:55,225
How did you end up here?

101
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:58,745
I came here on purpose.

102
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:00,825
I wanted to see you, Vin.

103
00:09:03,465 --> 00:09:04,985
Aunt La-Or feels the same.

104
00:09:05,625 --> 00:09:07,705
She misses you so much she’s fallen sick many times.

105
00:09:08,745 --> 00:09:09,785
She told me

106
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,305
to bring you home no matter what.

107
00:09:15,665 --> 00:09:17,144
But it’s not that easy, Dan.

108
00:09:17,145 --> 00:09:18,145
It’s not that hard, Vin.

109
00:09:19,265 --> 00:09:20,825
Just say the word,

110
00:09:21,945 --> 00:09:23,305
and I’ll take you out myself.

111
00:09:26,905 --> 00:09:28,265
Worry about saving yourself first.

112
00:09:29,225 --> 00:09:29,865
Get up.

113
00:09:29,866 --> 00:09:31,344
Hey! Let go of Vin!

114
00:09:31,345 --> 00:09:32,345
Stay out of this.

115
00:09:32,745 --> 00:09:33,745
Don’t touch my people.

116
00:09:34,585 --> 00:09:35,585
Vin.

117
00:09:36,145 --> 00:09:38,224
Can I have five minutes? Just five minutes.

118
00:09:38,225 --> 00:09:39,225
Five minutes?

119
00:09:39,945 --> 00:09:41,344
That could get you killed.

120
00:09:41,345 --> 00:09:42,465
What if someone else sees?

121
00:09:43,065 --> 00:09:44,185
Have you thought about that?

122
00:09:44,865 --> 00:09:45,865
Hey!

123
00:09:52,345 --> 00:09:53,545
What were you doing in there?

124
00:09:59,345 --> 00:10:00,545
Treating the prisoner's wound.

125
00:10:00,865 --> 00:10:01,905
I forgot something inside.

126
00:10:05,385 --> 00:10:06,385
Where is it then?

127
00:10:09,625 --> 00:10:10,625
It wasn't there.

128
00:10:13,025 --> 00:10:14,504
I dropped it somewhere else.

129
00:10:14,505 --> 00:10:16,145
Then why did you come together?

130
00:10:20,345 --> 00:10:21,665
And what rule says.

131
00:10:22,665 --> 00:10:23,905
Two people can’t come together?

132
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:54,225
What are you with that soldier?

133
00:10:55,105 --> 00:10:56,105
He was a neighbor.

134
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:58,345
We knew each other when we were kids.

135
00:10:59,145 --> 00:11:01,345
But he moved away when I was still in primary school.

136
00:11:02,425 --> 00:11:04,065
We never spoke again after that.

137
00:11:13,745 --> 00:11:15,545
That one is like an older brother.

138
00:11:21,745 --> 00:11:23,985
But this one isn’t.

139
00:11:28,505 --> 00:11:29,585
Promise me

140
00:11:30,665 --> 00:11:32,105
you won’t go see that soldier again.

141
00:11:34,625 --> 00:11:37,425
If anyone finds out, it’ll be very dangerous.

142
00:11:46,545 --> 00:11:47,745
Let me help you then.

143
00:11:50,905 --> 00:11:51,905
Get this over with.

144
00:12:23,865 --> 00:12:25,545
May I hold your hand?

145
00:12:37,625 --> 00:12:38,865
Who is Aunt La-Or?

146
00:12:39,745 --> 00:12:40,825
My mother.

147
00:12:45,385 --> 00:12:47,305
There’s still a lot about you that I don’t know.

148
00:12:48,705 --> 00:12:50,625
Not knowing isn’t a problem.

149
00:12:51,825 --> 00:12:53,505
We still have our whole lives together.

150
00:12:54,025 --> 00:12:57,305
I will tell you little by little, and you can teach me too.

151
00:13:03,185 --> 00:13:05,025
Everything I know, I’ve already taught you.

152
00:13:13,265 --> 00:13:15,785
Except this... You still have a lot to teach me.

153
00:13:28,305 --> 00:13:29,385
Pack up quickly.

154
00:13:37,985 --> 00:13:39,304
I just found out-

155
00:13:39,305 --> 00:13:42,064
-that grinding stones and mixing them with honey

156
00:13:42,065 --> 00:13:43,865
can make a color like this.

157
00:13:46,385 --> 00:13:47,865
If I put this on for Father to see,

158
00:13:48,625 --> 00:13:50,585
he’d definitely say I look cute.

159
00:14:00,225 --> 00:14:02,385
Comrade Ploeng hasn’t gone far at all.

160
00:14:03,185 --> 00:14:04,465
He only changed where he lives—.

161
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,705
Now he lives in Comrade Bai Tong’s heart.

162
00:14:08,985 --> 00:14:12,104
And you still have us, you have Comrade Saeng,

163
00:14:12,105 --> 00:14:14,505
and all the comrades beside you too.

164
00:14:25,185 --> 00:14:26,465
What are you doing here?

165
00:14:29,105 --> 00:14:30,105
Where is it?

166
00:14:36,745 --> 00:14:37,745
Comrade Fah,

167
00:14:37,945 --> 00:14:39,064
stop right now!

168
00:14:39,065 --> 00:14:40,144
Don’t take my father’s things!

169
00:14:40,145 --> 00:14:40,625
Hey!

170
00:14:40,625 --> 00:14:41,425
Don’t take them!

171
00:14:41,425 --> 00:14:42,425
Bai Tong!

172
00:14:44,105 --> 00:14:45,424
- Don't!
- Hey!

173
00:14:45,425 --> 00:14:46,585
This is not Comrade Ploeng’s?

174
00:14:47,465 --> 00:14:48,505
This belongs to the Party.

175
00:14:51,545 --> 00:14:52,625
And what is this, huh?

176
00:14:58,465 --> 00:14:59,545
That’s enough, Comrade Fah.

177
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:01,785
Wearing makeup and fixing hair like this...

178
00:15:01,825 --> 00:15:03,305
Looks like discipline is gone now.

179
00:15:04,105 --> 00:15:07,824
If I see it again, I won’t let it slide.

180
00:15:07,825 --> 00:15:09,864
In what capacity are you saying that?

181
00:15:09,865 --> 00:15:11,625
You're not the leader of the base.

182
00:15:12,465 --> 00:15:14,585
Comrade Ploeng would never threaten anyone like this.

183
00:15:31,505 --> 00:15:32,505
Sila.

184
00:15:38,225 --> 00:15:39,985
Mada.

185
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:48,905
Ravin.

186
00:15:49,705 --> 00:15:50,865
Chai Chan.

187
00:15:51,905 --> 00:15:53,345
Police Lieutenant...

188
00:15:54,105 --> 00:15:57,265
Rapee Chai Chan.

189
00:15:58,185 --> 00:15:59,304
I knew it.

190
00:15:59,305 --> 00:16:00,825
Comrade Fah.

191
00:16:04,225 --> 00:16:06,145
I just got word from Comrade Roong.

192
00:16:07,785 --> 00:16:08,785
What is it?

193
00:16:09,105 --> 00:16:10,825
Comrade Roong was captured by the soldiers.

194
00:16:11,025 --> 00:16:12,064
They sent word saying--

195
00:16:12,065 --> 00:16:13,505
That they want to exchange hostages.

196
00:16:17,705 --> 00:16:19,705
Go get Comrade Yue to the meeting right now.

197
00:16:25,465 --> 00:16:27,385
What in the actual fuck?

198
00:16:36,025 --> 00:16:38,945
You and Comrade Yue take control of them.

199
00:16:39,905 --> 00:16:41,104
Have armed men ready.

200
00:16:41,105 --> 00:16:42,185
Lock down the area.

201
00:16:43,665 --> 00:16:44,905
If they try anything dishonest,

202
00:16:45,545 --> 00:16:47,144
we’ll be ready to strike back.

203
00:16:47,145 --> 00:16:48,825
Everything must be finished tonight.

204
00:16:56,985 --> 00:16:57,985
Why?

205
00:16:59,345 --> 00:17:00,345
You have a problem?

206
00:17:05,225 --> 00:17:06,905
I’ll take care of it.

207
00:17:19,145 --> 00:17:20,145
Wait.

208
00:17:25,825 --> 00:17:26,545
You and Comrade Saeng

209
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,186
seem a little too close, don’t you think?

210
00:17:31,505 --> 00:17:33,385
Tell me then—what should I do?

211
00:17:47,905 --> 00:17:51,904
(Ravin ChaiChan)

212
00:17:51,905 --> 00:17:53,591
(Police Lieutenant Rapee ChaiChan
Mrs. La-Or Chai Chan)

213
00:17:57,385 --> 00:17:58,785
I’m going to take this all the way.

214
00:17:59,305 --> 00:18:00,584
Hey, where are you?

215
00:18:00,585 --> 00:18:01,305
Hey!

216
00:18:01,306 --> 00:18:03,184
Where’s your boss?

217
00:18:03,185 --> 00:18:05,344
- Bring your boss out here to talk to me!
- Stop, stop! Hey!

218
00:18:05,345 --> 00:18:06,864
This bastard right here!

219
00:18:06,865 --> 00:18:07,865
Stop!

220
00:18:08,745 --> 00:18:09,784
You know what?

221
00:18:09,785 --> 00:18:12,224
Because of you, our fathers died in prison for nothing.

222
00:18:12,225 --> 00:18:14,305
They never even got a chance to prove a damn thing.

223
00:18:18,625 --> 00:18:20,824
Hey! Hey! Hey!

224
00:18:20,825 --> 00:18:22,544
Hey, come out here and talk to me!

225
00:18:22,545 --> 00:18:23,865
Watch your mouth, kid.

226
00:18:24,465 --> 00:18:26,984
The lower court ruled that your fathers were guilty.

227
00:18:26,985 --> 00:18:28,184
Why blame the police?

228
00:18:28,185 --> 00:18:29,185
How can you say that?

229
00:18:29,905 --> 00:18:31,304
And if the court overturns it and says-

230
00:18:31,305 --> 00:18:32,344
-my father was innocent,

231
00:18:32,345 --> 00:18:32,985
how are you going to take responsibility?

232
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:36,304
The evidence was clear at the time, so I had to do my duty.

233
00:18:36,305 --> 00:18:37,504
You bastard!

234
00:18:37,505 --> 00:18:39,744
What the hell did you just say, you bastard?!

235
00:18:39,745 --> 00:18:40,825
Argh!

236
00:18:42,345 --> 00:18:45,545
Let me go! Let go! Let go!

237
00:18:47,305 --> 00:18:48,545
Get him out of here.

238
00:18:50,465 --> 00:18:52,265
Hey, stop!

239
00:18:54,745 --> 00:18:57,745
This isn’t over, bastard! This is not over!

240
00:18:58,185 --> 00:19:00,424
I'll get you back.

241
00:19:00,425 --> 00:19:01,665
Go!

242
00:19:03,985 --> 00:19:04,985
I’ll handle it myself.

243
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:08,905
How are you going to handle it? Tell me.

244
00:19:12,305 --> 00:19:13,664
Why the hell isn’t he here yet?

245
00:19:13,665 --> 00:19:14,665
This is taking forever.

246
00:19:17,185 --> 00:19:19,984
If we kill him, how are we any different from him?

247
00:19:19,985 --> 00:19:21,504
I don’t care whether we’re different or not.

248
00:19:21,505 --> 00:19:22,984
I only care that he pays for it.

249
00:19:22,985 --> 00:19:24,544
I’ll get rid of them all.

250
00:19:24,545 --> 00:19:26,065
Why are you chickening out now?

251
00:19:30,185 --> 00:19:31,305
He’s here!

252
00:19:32,585 --> 00:19:33,585
Ready?

253
00:19:33,785 --> 00:19:35,144
Wait... I’m not doing this anymore. Let’s go back.

254
00:19:35,145 --> 00:19:36,264
If you won’t do it, I will.

255
00:19:36,265 --> 00:19:37,265
You...

256
00:20:00,745 --> 00:20:01,905
Argh!

257
00:20:08,785 --> 00:20:09,785
Go to hell!

258
00:20:13,745 --> 00:20:14,745
Sin!

259
00:20:23,025 --> 00:20:23,625
You!

260
00:20:23,626 --> 00:20:24,705
Don’t hurt my friend!

261
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:28,505
Don’t hurt my friend!

262
00:20:57,105 --> 00:21:01,185
Aagh! Aagh! Aagh!

263
00:21:21,745 --> 00:21:24,384
Sin! Sin! Sin! Look at me!

264
00:21:24,385 --> 00:21:25,984
Look at me, Sin!

265
00:21:25,985 --> 00:21:27,265
Sin, look at me!

266
00:21:29,385 --> 00:21:30,385
Run!

267
00:21:30,545 --> 00:21:31,545
Run!

268
00:21:31,625 --> 00:21:33,505
Run! Go!

269
00:21:33,985 --> 00:21:34,985
Go!

270
00:21:36,905 --> 00:21:37,905
Go!

271
00:21:49,585 --> 00:21:50,585
Sin!

272
00:21:52,465 --> 00:21:53,465
Or do you want him to find out

273
00:21:53,466 --> 00:21:54,786
that you and I killed his father,

274
00:21:55,625 --> 00:21:56,985
and wait for him to come after us?

275
00:22:02,785 --> 00:22:03,825
I’m telling you,

276
00:22:05,545 --> 00:22:08,145
we should nip it in the bud.

277
00:22:16,745 --> 00:22:17,745
Nop.

278
00:22:21,385 --> 00:22:23,185
Whether you want to be the leader of the base

279
00:22:24,945 --> 00:22:26,824
or whatever else you want to do,

280
00:22:26,825 --> 00:22:27,825
I don’t care.

281
00:22:29,865 --> 00:22:30,865
But this matter...

282
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,745
Let me handle it myself.

283
00:23:19,945 --> 00:23:21,025
Hey!

284
00:23:34,585 --> 00:23:35,585
What’s wrong with you?

285
00:23:36,465 --> 00:23:37,745
Why did you hurt yourself?

286
00:23:49,865 --> 00:23:51,785
Are you so jealous that you ended up crying?

287
00:23:53,705 --> 00:23:55,945
Why are you acting like a child?

288
00:23:56,865 --> 00:23:58,905
I had a small argument with Comrade Fah.

289
00:24:00,225 --> 00:24:01,305
It’s nothing.

290
00:24:07,825 --> 00:24:09,065
Come on, I’ll treat your wound.

291
00:24:15,305 --> 00:24:16,305
Go back first.

292
00:24:17,185 --> 00:24:18,665
I’ll follow after you.

293
00:25:13,705 --> 00:25:14,865
When you get out,

294
00:25:16,065 --> 00:25:17,465
don’t ever come back here again.

295
00:25:22,305 --> 00:25:23,945
Whether I come back or not, I don’t know.

296
00:25:25,385 --> 00:25:27,705
But I’m definitely taking my person with me.

297
00:25:35,625 --> 00:25:36,945
Does Vin know

298
00:25:37,825 --> 00:25:39,105
that he belongs to you?

299
00:25:41,585 --> 00:25:43,065
Anything that’s in the wrong place

300
00:25:44,865 --> 00:25:46,305
doesn’t stay there for long.

301
00:25:47,825 --> 00:25:49,865
If fooling yourself makes you happy, then go ahead.

302
00:27:06,145 --> 00:27:08,105
Why are you sleeping here?

303
00:27:12,145 --> 00:27:13,145
I was worried.

304
00:27:14,025 --> 00:27:15,945
Did you have a serious fight with Comrade Fah?

305
00:27:19,985 --> 00:27:21,065
Go get some sleep.

306
00:27:26,865 --> 00:27:28,545
I took this from the medical hut.

307
00:27:30,185 --> 00:27:31,585
I need to hurry and return it.

308
00:27:39,985 --> 00:27:40,985
Come here.

309
00:28:40,625 --> 00:28:43,185
Even now, you’re still shy?

310
00:28:54,025 --> 00:28:55,865
Did you ever feel so happy--

311
00:28:58,185 --> 00:29:00,345
That you're afraid it ends badly?

312
00:29:01,425 --> 00:29:04,265
People either part while alive... or part by death.

313
00:29:05,465 --> 00:29:07,145
And we never know when we’ll part.

314
00:29:08,065 --> 00:29:09,424
If we spend all our time being afraid

315
00:29:09,425 --> 00:29:10,785
until we can’t do anything at all,

316
00:29:11,425 --> 00:29:12,745
wouldn’t it be more regretful

317
00:29:14,025 --> 00:29:15,585
if we never tried with all our heart?

318
00:29:28,465 --> 00:29:29,705
Then what should I do?

319
00:29:32,665 --> 00:29:34,865
You have to keep collecting happiness little by little.

320
00:29:35,385 --> 00:29:36,305
Like this—

321
00:29:36,306 --> 00:29:37,865
I'm doing it right now.

322
00:30:13,105 --> 00:30:14,105
That’s enough.

323
00:30:18,065 --> 00:30:20,345
And you don’t need to be jealous of that soldier anymore.

324
00:30:22,105 --> 00:30:23,385
I love only this person.

325
00:31:26,185 --> 00:31:27,745
The murderer is coming.

326
00:32:04,585 --> 00:32:05,585
I’m sorry.

327
00:32:56,785 --> 00:32:57,905
Go tell Vin

328
00:32:58,585 --> 00:33:00,545
that the person who loves him is waiting outside.

329
00:33:08,225 --> 00:33:09,305
You’re alright, aren’t you?

330
00:34:05,825 --> 00:34:07,824
What did that soldier say just now?

331
00:34:07,825 --> 00:34:08,985
Did you get what he said?

332
00:34:17,785 --> 00:34:19,745
Oh, Comrade Saeng, how did you get here?

333
00:34:24,785 --> 00:34:25,785
So?

334
00:34:26,305 --> 00:34:27,425
When did it start?

335
00:34:35,025 --> 00:34:36,505
Can you please not tell anyone?

336
00:34:37,865 --> 00:34:38,665
I don’t want Comrade Saeng

337
00:34:38,666 --> 00:34:40,066
to get into trouble because of me.

338
00:34:43,385 --> 00:34:46,024
The good thing about being a courier, Comrade,

339
00:34:46,025 --> 00:34:47,624
is first of all,

340
00:34:47,625 --> 00:34:49,264
I run everywhere in the forest,

341
00:34:49,265 --> 00:34:50,785
outside the forest, and in the city.

342
00:34:52,105 --> 00:34:54,424
I meet all kinds of people everywhere.

343
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:57,584
Whether it’s couples with an age gap and things like that,

344
00:34:57,585 --> 00:34:59,465
or men who like men, women who like women...

345
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:02,545
I honestly don’t think there’s anything strange about it.

346
00:35:04,625 --> 00:35:05,625
And...

347
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,265
do you despise it, Comrade?

348
00:35:10,985 --> 00:35:13,945
I think it’s simply about two people loving each other.

349
00:35:15,265 --> 00:35:16,465
There’s nothing ugly about it.

350
00:35:18,425 --> 00:35:19,505
So what now?

351
00:35:20,545 --> 00:35:21,945
Anything to say?

352
00:35:22,705 --> 00:35:24,545
Do you love each other that much, huh?

353
00:35:28,305 --> 00:35:30,384
Wow... seeing Comrade Yue blush like this,

354
00:35:30,385 --> 00:35:31,904
I can die with my eyes closed now.

355
00:35:31,905 --> 00:35:32,905
I’m off.

356
00:35:34,145 --> 00:35:35,345
Hurry and catch up.

357
00:35:36,865 --> 00:35:38,505
Comrade Phu Pha.

358
00:36:03,145 --> 00:36:04,145
Dan.

359
00:36:04,225 --> 00:36:05,225
Father.

360
00:36:08,065 --> 00:36:09,065
How did you get here?

361
00:36:09,705 --> 00:36:11,904
Whatever you’re planning to do, just tell me?

362
00:36:11,905 --> 00:36:12,945
Is that so hard?

363
00:36:16,305 --> 00:36:17,305
If...

364
00:36:17,825 --> 00:36:20,785
If I had told you I was going in there to become a hostage,

365
00:36:21,425 --> 00:36:22,585
would you have let me go?

366
00:36:23,345 --> 00:36:24,745
And what were you doing in there?

367
00:36:26,305 --> 00:36:27,505
Helping the students.

368
00:36:28,705 --> 00:36:31,145
There are students in the jungle all over the country.

369
00:36:31,785 --> 00:36:33,825
But you deliberately chose to go to that base.

370
00:36:35,145 --> 00:36:36,504
Does this have anything to do with the information.

371
00:36:36,505 --> 00:36:37,984
I asked you to investigate before?

372
00:36:37,985 --> 00:36:39,385
Um... no, it’s not related, Father.

373
00:36:41,545 --> 00:36:43,264
As for Baan Saeng Dao Base,

374
00:36:43,265 --> 00:36:45,145
it’s the base closest to the main headquarters.

375
00:36:45,545 --> 00:36:47,825
If this place falls, the rest will collapse too.

376
00:36:48,905 --> 00:36:49,905
I just wanted to-

377
00:36:50,185 --> 00:36:51,864
-settle things properly, that’s all.

378
00:36:51,865 --> 00:36:53,305
Don’t think about attacking anymore.

379
00:36:54,225 --> 00:36:55,785
Right now, the higher-ups have a policy

380
00:36:56,225 --> 00:36:57,465
to bring the students back in.

381
00:36:57,905 --> 00:36:59,145
Bring the students back?

382
00:36:59,905 --> 00:37:00,505
Yes.

383
00:37:00,505 --> 00:37:01,505
I mean...

384
00:37:02,305 --> 00:37:04,465
Does that mean we’re not going to fight anymore?

385
00:37:05,185 --> 00:37:06,185
Yes.

386
00:37:06,825 --> 00:37:07,865
The leaders have realized-

387
00:37:08,665 --> 00:37:10,745
-that chasing each other like this

388
00:37:11,785 --> 00:37:14,105
is the same as killing our own children and grandchildren.

389
00:37:14,265 --> 00:37:15,825
Bringing them back out of the forest

390
00:37:16,985 --> 00:37:19,265
will make them useful to the nation.

391
00:37:28,545 --> 00:37:30,784
Why are you making dots like that, Comrade Saeng?

392
00:37:30,785 --> 00:37:32,665
I’m not a spotted deer.

393
00:37:39,985 --> 00:37:41,625
A spotted deer or a cat?

394
00:37:43,905 --> 00:37:45,985
Then do it properly, Comrade Saeng.

395
00:37:47,225 --> 00:37:48,624
Stay still. I’ll fix it.

396
00:37:48,625 --> 00:37:53,984
Comrade Bai Tong’s flower crown is finished.

397
00:37:53,985 --> 00:37:56,225
How is it? Look in the mirror.

398
00:37:58,825 --> 00:38:00,145
So pretty.

399
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:04,545
Of course. Cause I made it.

400
00:38:09,585 --> 00:38:11,825
What are you doing?

401
00:38:12,785 --> 00:38:14,985
The order appointing the new base leader has arrived.

402
00:38:27,905 --> 00:38:29,744
I feel greatly honored

403
00:38:29,745 --> 00:38:31,785
to be trusted with taking care of this base.

404
00:38:32,465 --> 00:38:35,385
And I promise that everything will remain the same.

405
00:38:36,425 --> 00:38:38,344
But some loose matters may be adjusted-

406
00:38:38,345 --> 00:38:40,385
-to better follow the rules.

407
00:38:49,945 --> 00:38:51,704
And the rules begin now!

408
00:38:51,705 --> 00:38:54,824
When the leader is speaking, everyone should listen,

409
00:38:54,825 --> 00:38:56,625
not turn and look elsewhere.

410
00:38:57,705 --> 00:38:59,545
And I’d like two or three comrades

411
00:38:59,665 --> 00:39:00,904
to help me move Comrade Ploeng’s

412
00:39:00,905 --> 00:39:01,945
belongings from the house.

413
00:39:05,185 --> 00:39:06,185
Because I’ll likely-

414
00:39:06,705 --> 00:39:08,025
-be moving in there

415
00:39:08,985 --> 00:39:10,464
as required by the position.

416
00:39:10,465 --> 00:39:12,105
I’ll speak on behalf of Comrade Bai Tong.

417
00:39:12,345 --> 00:39:13,584
Comrade Bai Tong has lived there since birth.

418
00:39:13,585 --> 00:39:14,585
And?

419
00:39:14,745 --> 00:39:15,705
If moved out now,

420
00:39:15,706 --> 00:39:17,466
Comrade Bai Tong won’t be able to handle it.

421
00:39:17,945 --> 00:39:18,945
That’s right.

422
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:20,385
Let Comrade Bai Tong rest first.

423
00:39:20,945 --> 00:39:22,344
Let her recover emotionally first.

424
00:39:22,345 --> 00:39:23,105
No.

425
00:39:23,105 --> 00:39:24,065
It must be now.

426
00:39:24,066 --> 00:39:25,424
- Why?
- Damn it.

427
00:39:25,425 --> 00:39:26,504
You really meddle too much.

428
00:39:26,505 --> 00:39:27,624
You two, follow me.

429
00:39:27,625 --> 00:39:28,625
Now.

430
00:39:29,025 --> 00:39:30,025
Hey!

431
00:39:43,265 --> 00:39:44,984
You two, move everything out.

432
00:39:44,985 --> 00:39:46,505
Don’t leave a single piece behind. Go!

433
00:39:47,465 --> 00:39:48,905
Don’t take my father’s things!

434
00:39:49,745 --> 00:39:50,945
- Hey!
- No!

435
00:39:51,585 --> 00:39:53,905
- No! Where are you taking my father’s things?!
- Bai Tong.

436
00:39:59,625 --> 00:40:01,144
Don’t take my father’s things!

437
00:40:01,145 --> 00:40:02,145
Hey!

438
00:40:07,065 --> 00:40:09,104
Don’t take anything away!

439
00:40:09,105 --> 00:40:09,865
Let go!

440
00:40:09,865 --> 00:40:10,865
Bai Tong!

441
00:40:10,865 --> 00:40:11,865
Bai Tong!

442
00:40:12,305 --> 00:40:13,704
You won’t even spare a child, huh?

443
00:40:13,705 --> 00:40:15,745
You really love meddling in my business, don’t you?

444
00:40:24,945 --> 00:40:26,265
This is already more than enough.

445
00:40:27,025 --> 00:40:28,264
Don’t make this a bigger deal.

446
00:40:28,265 --> 00:40:29,705
Why are you staring at me like that?

447
00:40:29,825 --> 00:40:31,465
Got a problem? Huh?

448
00:40:37,185 --> 00:40:38,185
Bai Tong!

449
00:40:39,225 --> 00:40:41,065
Aah! You little brat!

450
00:40:46,745 --> 00:40:47,984
Wearing makeup and fixing your hair like-

451
00:40:47,985 --> 00:40:49,665
-this is against Party rules, understand?

452
00:40:55,665 --> 00:40:56,665
Son of a bitch!

453
00:40:56,665 --> 00:40:57,665
Bai Tong!

454
00:41:01,305 --> 00:41:02,505
Ouch!

455
00:41:06,545 --> 00:41:07,545
- Bai Tong!
- Sin.

456
00:41:07,825 --> 00:41:08,945
If you don’t stop right now,

457
00:41:09,825 --> 00:41:10,864
you’ll see.

458
00:41:10,865 --> 00:41:11,945
You...

459
00:41:33,265 --> 00:41:34,424
Am I pretty, Father?

460
00:41:34,425 --> 00:41:36,225
Wow...

461
00:41:36,905 --> 00:41:38,745
very pretty, my dear.

462
00:41:39,865 --> 00:41:41,624
But you know

463
00:41:41,625 --> 00:41:44,985
you can’t wear flowers like that and go walking outside.

464
00:41:46,065 --> 00:41:48,064
But why, Father?

465
00:41:48,065 --> 00:41:49,905
I can let only Comrade Ying see it.

466
00:41:52,025 --> 00:41:55,545
If every woman comrade here wanted to be pretty like you,

467
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:59,185
and wanted to wear flowers like you, every one of them,

468
00:42:00,225 --> 00:42:01,705
what do you think would happen?

469
00:42:05,025 --> 00:42:06,624
If all the women comrades

470
00:42:06,625 --> 00:42:08,384
picked flowers to wear every day,

471
00:42:08,385 --> 00:42:10,265
then there wouldn’t be any flowers left, right?

472
00:42:11,545 --> 00:42:12,705
That’s true.

473
00:42:13,585 --> 00:42:14,784
Flowers...

474
00:42:14,785 --> 00:42:17,544
they’re useful because they’re beautiful.

475
00:42:17,545 --> 00:42:19,545
And they have other uses too.

476
00:42:20,345 --> 00:42:21,625
But here,

477
00:42:22,225 --> 00:42:24,745
I see them as something unnecessary.

478
00:42:26,465 --> 00:42:27,865
Bai Tong, my child.

479
00:42:28,905 --> 00:42:30,744
I want you to be a good example

480
00:42:30,745 --> 00:42:32,185
to the women comrades here.

481
00:42:33,265 --> 00:42:34,625
Live simply,

482
00:42:35,105 --> 00:42:36,665
and not extravagantly.

483
00:42:37,825 --> 00:42:39,305
You understand me, don’t you?

484
00:42:46,025 --> 00:42:48,024
Then I’ll pick flowers from the ground-

485
00:42:48,025 --> 00:42:49,425
-and wear them only for Father.

486
00:42:50,865 --> 00:42:52,265
That's my girl.

487
00:42:52,865 --> 00:42:54,105
Very good.

488
00:42:54,865 --> 00:42:57,185
Very good for understanding things so easily.

489
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:22,305
You hit me that hard...

490
00:43:22,825 --> 00:43:24,425
you really hate me that much, don’t you?

491
00:43:24,665 --> 00:43:26,425
I only asked what you two are to each other.

